      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dances:**\n   Each man danced with exactly 3 women. Since there are 12 men, the total number of dances (where each dance involves one man and one woman) is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of women:**\n   Each woman danced with exactly 2 men. Let \\( W \\) be the number of women at the party. Each woman contributes to 2 dances, so the total number of dances can also be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   W \\text{ women} \\times 2 \\text{ dances per woman} = 2W \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n   We know from step 1 that the total number of dances is 36, so we set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   2W = 36\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( W \\):**\n   \\[\n   W = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
